// §6.8: "An identifier shall be used to declare only one item within a scope."
// duplicate_declaration_rejected.va pins two VARIABLES; the sentence says ITEM,
// and a parameter and a net are items of the module scope as much as a variable
// is (§6.8 lists what opens a new scope — modules, named blocks, analog
// functions, generate blocks — and a second declaration is not on it).
//
// A net and a variable named `x` in one module: two kinds of item, one
// identifier. Renaming the variable makes the file legal. The net is a `wire`
// with no discipline on purpose: a discipline declaration beside a variable
// attaches the discipline to it (§7.8's connect modules write `reg out;
// ddiscrete out;`), which is one item, not two.
//
//! lrm 6.8
//! reject E0362
`include "disciplines.vams"
module ch6_net_variable_same_name(p);
  inout p; electrical p;
  wire x;
  real x;
  analog I(p) <+ V(p);
endmodule
